# The app uses a HASH router, so every route is /#/learn, /#/progress and so on,
# and the server only ever serves one document. This catch-all is therefore
# defensive rather than required today: it means a mistyped or shared deep path
# lands on the app's own 404 screen — which offers real destinations — instead of
# Cloudflare's.
#
# It also means that if the router is ever moved to history mode, deep links keep
# working rather than 404ing on the first visit.
/*  /index.html  200
